Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:39:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 136/144] GreatDANE: harden the Pepecoin publisher check;
 reject NGD bypasses (round 4i)

The 4h exemption in trademark_userfacing_check.py was bypassable. In the
six publisher files (both module.ver files, both exe manifests, greatdane
branding.nsi, and shared.nsh) there are no exemptions: line continuations
are joined and NSIS ${NAME} references are resolved, then any Pepecoin
publisher/company/copyright string fails. Elsewhere, comments (#, ;, //,
<!-- -->) are stripped first, and only a line whose key is the vendor
(MOZ_APP_VENDOR=... or the configure vendor setting) is exempt.

Company and publisher values (WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME, CompanyName,
ARPPublisher) must be non-empty and not "Mozilla". The official shared.nsh
fallback Publisher "Mozilla" is unchanged.

Fixtures under greatdane/tests/fixtures/pepecoin-publisher/ (not shipped)
cover NGD's five bypasses plus an empty company and ARPPublisher "Mozilla".
All of those must be rejected; the real tree must pass.

MOZ_APP_VENDOR "Pepecoin" stays as an internal identifier; changing it
would move profiles. The publisher name remains owner-pending.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
